@* Disabled on the control AND on the field: the control stops accepting input, and the field
   greys its label to say so. Upstream writes exactly this pair — a disabled box under a
   full-strength label reads as a box that is merely empty. *@
<Field Disabled Class="w-[420px]">
    <FieldLabel For="ta-disabled">Message</FieldLabel>
    <Textarea id="ta-disabled" rows="3" placeholder="Type your message here." disabled />
</Field>
